<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9445] Use valid tag for page write unlock while reading cold page from disk.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9445</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The problem arises when passing pageId with not actual page rotation tag to org.apache.ignite.internal.processors.cache.persistence.pagemem.PageMemoryImpl#acquirePage(int, long, boolean).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It&apos;s not possible in advance to know the actual value without reading stored page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Such scenario may lead to locked forever page if passed and persisted tags are different.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Solution - unlock the page using actual(persisted) tag value.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
